> The key to great stuffed eggplant is removing excess moisture from the eggplant before filling—salted eggplant weeps out its bitter compounds and water, preventing the fried result from being soggy. The pork filling should be seasoned boldly; the mild eggplant needs the savory filling to balance it.

== Prepare the Eggplant ==

Slice @Chinese eggplants{500%g} into 1 cm thick rounds. If the eggplants are very large, cut in half lengthwise first.

Lay the slices on a wire rack or plate and sprinkle both sides generously with @salt{1%tsp}. Let sit for ~{20%minutes}.

This draws out moisture and removes bitterness. The slices will look wilted and weeping—pat completely dry with paper towels before using.

== Make the Filling ==

In a bowl, combine @ground pork{200%g} with:
- @Shaoxing wine{1%tsp}
- @light soy sauce{1%tsp}
- @salt{¼%tsp}
- @white pepper{⅛%tsp}
- @ginger{½%tsp} (minced)
- @scallions{1%stalk} (minced)
- @sesame oil{½%tsp}

Mix in one direction until the pork becomes slightly sticky and cohesive.

== Assemble the Eggplant ==

Set up your breading station:
- @all-purpose flour{60%g} (for dusting)
- @eggs{2} (beaten)
- @breadcrumbs{100%g}

Dust each eggplant slice lightly with flour. Place a tablespoon of the pork filling on one slice, then top with another slice to create a sandwich. Press edges firmly to seal.

Dip each assembled sandwich into the beaten egg, letting excess drip off. Coat with breadcrumbs, pressing firmly to adhere.

== Fry the Eggplant ==

Heat @oil{480%ml} in a #wok{} or deep pot to 180°C (350°F).

Working in batches, carefully lower the eggplant sandwiches and fry for ~{3-4%minutes} per side until deep golden brown and crispy.

Use a spider or slotted spoon to turn gently. The filling needs time to cook through without burning the exterior.

Remove and drain on a wire rack set over a baking sheet. Preheat oven to 90°C (200°F) to keep warm while you finish frying.

== Make the Dipping Sauce ==

While frying, make the sauce:

In a small bowl, combine:
- @tomato sauce{4%tbsp}
- @rice vinegar{1%tbsp}
- @sugar{1%tsp}
- @salt{¼%tsp}
- @sesame oil{¼%tsp}

Stir until sugar dissolves. Adjust to taste—this should be tangy with a hint of sweetness.

== Serve ==

Arrange the fried eggplant on a platter. Garnish with @sliced scallions{1%stalk}.

Serve immediately with the dipping sauce alongside. The contrast between the crispy exterior and creamy, savory filling is what makes this dish special.